                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">0bfdfbc4-1cfb-44fa-aa9f-aee98c0e71f4</item>
                    <item name="Italic" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Scribble</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Scribble</item>
                    <item name="Size" type_name="gh_single" type_code="5">9</item>
                    <item name="Text" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">STEP 4  -  Give floors thickness
Goal: each floor outline pushed down into a slab.
Idea: Extrude pushes a curve along a vector. A closed outline
   becomes the edge of a slab.
Watch for: The direction is a vector, not a number.
Wire check: outlines -&gt; B (base), vector -&gt; D (direction).</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="1">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="2">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
